------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

None of these is copied into git or passed on with the app; each is installed or already present on the
laptop, outside the app's own environment. Read on 2026-11-27 by the S6 builder at the source named.

ST Edge AI Core (the N6 compiler, `stedgeai`) — STMicroelectronics, not open source.
  In use: 4.0.0 (v4.0.0-20500), inside OpenMV's SDK 1.6.0. Its terms are SLA0104 Rev1 / June 2024 (the SDK's
  `stedgeai/Package_license.html`; the same text is written as LICENSE.txt next to every model it generates).
  Read but not installed: 4.1.0, under SLA0044 Rev 7 / February 2026 ("Ultimate Liberty"; ST's docs,
  stm32ai-cs.st.com/assets/embedded-docs/Package_license.html). Nick said yes to ST's terms on 2026-11-27
  (docs/source/build2_spec.md, answer 15).
  What both say that matters here: the software and anything derived from it "must be used and execute solely
  and exclusively on or in combination with a processing unit device manufactured by or for
  STMicroelectronics" (SLA0044's words; SLA0104 says the same with "a device or a processing unit device
  manufactured by or for ST"); it must not be mixed into anything in a way that puts it under an open-source licence;
  passing it on in binary form, other than inside an ST device, must carry ST's notice and disclaimer.
  SLA0104 adds export rules (no supply to Russia, Belarus or sanctioned countries; records of anything
  passed on, open to ST's audit).
  For this project: the compiler runs on the laptop to make model files for the STM32N6 only, which is the
  permitted use. A model file made for the N6 contains ST's code and runs only on the N6; the Pi and the AE3
  get their own files from other tools. Nothing of ST's goes into git. Copies of both texts are in
  `<tools_dir>/licences/`.

Arm Vela (the AE3 compiler, `ethos-u-vela` 5.0.0; 5.2.0 for comparison) — Apache-2.0 (PyPI metadata,
  pypi.org/pypi/ethos-u-vela/5.0.0/json).

OpenMV firmware tree, commit 7d4dbf7 (`tools/modelc.py`, `tools/vela.ini`, `lib/stai/scripts/neuralart.json`
  and its memory-pool file; read in place from Nick's checkout) — MIT (the header of `tools/modelc.py`:
  "This work is licensed under the MIT license").

OpenMV SDK 1.6.0 (linux-x86_64; holds ST Edge AI Core, Vela 5.0.0 and the Arm GNU toolchain that ST's
  relocatable step links with) and the `firmware-builder` container image — set up by Nick's earlier work
